  "notes": [
   "Step 1 parts are unchanged. The micro-USB power source stays out because neither the circuit image nor the schematic shows it.",
   "The battery's JST PH plug goes into the board's JST connector. The catalogue has no JST port on the MKR WiFi 1010, so I mapped battery + to BATT and battery - to GND. The schematic shows both battery leads going to the JST block.",
   "The pushbutton straddles the breadboard centre gap in column 8. I put its legs in 8b.f and 10b.f (side 1, top) and 8t.e and 10t.e (side 2, bottom). The image shows only the column-8 legs being used.",
   "The black wire runs from board GND to 8b.g, on the same strip as side 1 of the button. The yellow wire runs from D8 (MOSI) to 8t.d, on the same strip as side 2. Pressing the button joins D8 to GND.",
   "The button has no external resistor, as in the tutorial. The sketch's wake-up interrupt on pin 8 presumably relies on an internal pull-up.",
   "The catalogue's breadboard banks are named 't' for rows a-e and 'b' for rows f-j. The image draws rows j-f at the top and e-a at the bottom, but the names follow the catalogue."
  ]
 },
